<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2013/05/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <!-- The XrmToolBox Tool Library package. <version> must equal the assembly version in
         src\MyscotekDataCopier\Properties\AssemblyInfo.cs, or the Tool Library offers an update
         forever: build-package.ps1 refuses to pack when they differ. -->
    <id>Myscotek.DataCopier</id>
    <version>1.2026.10.1</version>
    <title>Data Copier</title>
    <authors>Myscotek</authors>
    <owners>Myscotek</owners>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <license type="expression">MIT</license>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/scottm1985/DataCopier</projectUrl>
    <!-- The Tool Library shows iconUrl; NuGet clients show the packed icon (iconUrl alone is deprecated). -->
    <iconUrl>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/scottm1985/DataCopier/main/images/icon-128.png</iconUrl>
    <icon>images/icon-128.png</icon>
    <repository type="git" url="https://github.com/scottm1985/DataCopier" />
    <summary>Copies selected Dataverse / Dynamics 365 records to another environment with the same GUIDs, with the records their lookups point at and, optionally, their child records.</summary>
    <description>
      XrmToolBox tool. Pick an entity and a view in the source environment, tick the records you want and copy
      them to a destination environment (Dataverse online or Dynamics 365 on-premises 9.x), keeping the same GUIDs.
      The records they point at through lookups are copied first, as deep as needed, so the lookups still resolve;
      optionally their child records (the subgrids of each entity, or the 1:N relationships you choose) come along
      too. Records that already exist are updated or skipped by clear rules, users, teams and currencies are never
      created, virtual tables are only checked, closing states (won opportunities, resolved cases and so on) are
      applied with the platform's close messages, and a dry run shows everything that would happen. Every step is
      written to a colour-coded log.
    </description>
    <releaseNotes>
      1.2026.10.1 - first public release.
      - Copy the ticked records of any view with the same GUIDs; a selected record that exists is updated.
      - Copy N:1 relationships (lookups): the records they point at are created first, recursively; an existing
        one is skipped; circular references are backfilled.
      - Copy 1:N relationships (subgrids): child records, recursively; per entity, the main-form subgrids or the
        relationships ticked in the Relationships picker.
      - Users, teams, business units, the organisation and currencies are never created; virtual tables are
        checked by id and never written.
      - Closing states applied once the record's tree is done, with the close messages (win/lose opportunity,
        close case, win/close quote, cancel/fulfil order).
      - Dry run, preserve created on, bypass custom plugins (online), personal views, paging, client-side filter.
      - Colour-coded log with copy and save, a summary and the errors of every run.
    </releaseNotes>
    <copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Myscotek</copyright>
    <!-- The "XrmToolBox" tag is what the Tool Library looks for. -->
    <tags>XrmToolBox Plugins Dataverse Dynamics365 Data Copy Records Migration Myscotek</tags>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency id="XrmToolBox" version="1.2025.10.74" />
    </dependencies>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <!-- XrmToolBox installs lib\net48\Plugins\* into its Plugins folder. Only the tool's own assembly
         ships: XrmToolBox provides the XrmToolBox, McTools, Dataverse SDK and Newtonsoft assemblies. -->
    <file src="src\MyscotekDataCopier\bin\Release\MyscotekDataCopier.dll" target="lib\net48\Plugins" />
    <file src="images\icon-128.png" target="images\" />
  </files>
</package>
